# Story page: treasure
# {name} becomes the snake's name. Paragraphs are separated by a blank line.
title = The Vault
---
Behind a door heavier than a Monday morning lies the Vault, where everything is oversized: the apples, the popsicles, and most especially the danger.

{name} had never felt so small, which was reasonable, because it had shrunk. How it shrank I cannot tell you, and I urge you not to ask anyone else either.

On the floor lay a single golden scale, still warm, bearing {name}'s exact pattern. This is not, I assure you, suspicious in the least. I am lying. It is extremely suspicious.
